  // "jobs": each part's job. A room is "w" x "d" m (its open front faces the route) and a list of slots, "job[*count]@place[r][:x,z] example":
  // B on the back wall, L / R along the left / right walls (as seen from the route), W hung on the back wall, C free-standing with its centre
  // x, z m from the back-left corner; "r" turns the piece a quarter. Each slot takes the most-stocked part of its job that fits; the first slot
  // is the room's key: with none of it in stock the room is passed over. The example is the part the layout drew; it is a note only.
  // "departments" run along the route in this order: their rooms whose key is in stock, then a product wall of every part in stock of "jobs"
